AgentDrop — one set of working rules across Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode,
Command Code and Gemini CLI, without overwriting harness-specific instructions.

Usage:
  agentdrop                    Bootstrap/sync the current directory after confirmation
  agentdrop --install          Install command + sync global rules
  agentdrop sync               Re-sync global rules after editing COMMON.md
  agentdrop edit               Open the master COMMON.md
  agentdrop status [PATH]      The owner's board: waits for you, running, done, next (--json)
  agentdrop claim B41          Claim a ticket for this session (docs/.claims/, not in git)
  agentdrop release B41        Release it at the end of the pass
  agentdrop store import       Copy this project's tickets and questions into the task store
  agentdrop store check        Show where the task store and the project's markdown differ
  agentdrop task take [B12]    In a project whose tasks live in the store (`tasks.<folder> = store`
                               in the config): take one task; also `task show|state|ask|comment|
                               handin|new|where`

Project skeleton (docs/, charter, review-intake skill, docs guard) lives at:
  ~/.agentdrop/kit/   — CHARTER.md goes into AGENTS.md, other files are copied if missing
  agentdrop /path/to/project   Bootstrap/sync a project
  agentdrop .                  Bootstrap/sync current project without the extra cwd prompt
  agentdrop --dry-run [PATH]   Preview changes; defaults to the current directory
  agentdrop --docs MODE PATH   Docs in the code repo (track), a local .git-docs (separate)
                               or nowhere (local); asked on the first run, then remembered
  agentdrop --research PATH    Also turn on research mode (registries of asks, hypotheses
                               and claims; skeptic and acceptance agents). First setup asks.
  agentdrop --no-research PATH Turn research mode off (removes its block, keeps the files)

The master rules live at:
  ~/.agentdrop/COMMON.md
"""

